{
  "id": "magic_pulse",
  "title": "Magic Pulses",
  "item": "omnira:pulse_accumulator_orb",
  "icon": "omnira:mana_engine",
  "recipes": false,
  "text": [
    "Potential is measured in MPU. Align source outputs with machine inputs, or connect through Arcane Wires and Accumulator Orbs. Sources combine; insufficient potential for all base demands pauses the entire network.",
    "Reserve base demands first, then grant acceleration in connection order, up to 8x. New loads reclaim extra reservations from newer machines first.",
    "Native machines prioritize pulses, then stress, then electricity. Sustained FE/second is equivalent to MPU, is consumed even while idle, and must continue without stored-energy operation after input stops. Accelerating machines scale with input up to their existing limits; extra power does not accelerate the Infused Crystal Furnace. Insufficient pulses cannot fall back to external power.",
    "All shaft inputs, including orbs, require at least 16 rpm in either direction; slower inputs are rejected without stress use. Arcane Assembly Benches and Infused Crystal Anvils use 16 x |RPM| SU. Each Reaction Pool inlet uses 32 x |RPM| SU; both inputs combine for efficiency, capped at 8x.",
    "Direct kinetic or electrical connections change source effects to 16 rpm rotation or electricity. 1 MPU equals 1 SU or 1 FE/second. Spacetime Ports retain source pulse effects and convert remotely.",
    "Stand in the cell directly beside a pulse output to absorb one tenth of its unused potential as mana each second, rounded up. Machines have priority; players share the remainder and count as source usage. Kinetic and electrical output modes cannot charge players.",
    "Pulses can overfill mana. If mana already exceeds 150% of its limit, the next input triggers a radius-5 magic blast: living creatures take 20 magic damage and entities are pushed away; blocks and items survive. Only the triggering player receives Weakness II and Slowness II for 3 minutes. Excess mana vents back to the normal limit."
  ],
